--- !u!114 &418895210
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 418895208}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7d20f73aabcb4cfbaac49363662be3e1, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueController
  currentDialogueIndex: 0
  textStartOffset: 0
  dialogues:
  - texts:
    - Hail!
    - Quite a surprise to encounter another out here. Are you attempting the climb
      as well?
    - I had hoped to reach the Summit by now... but the terrain is more difficult
      than I anticipated.
    - It seems I still have much to learn!
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    resetDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - My name is Rheal, by the way. I am attempting my Mynkecha.
    - ...
    - I assume you don't know what that is.
    - Completely understandable. The <color=#D0C4FF>Way of the Lotus</color> is,
      sadly, mostly lost to time. But some still pursue it.
    - If you'd like, I would be happy to share my knowledge with you.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    resetDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - Long ago, there lived on the Mountain a sect of spiritual minds who are now
      known as the Lotus Monks.
    - The Monks believed the Mountain's terrain is holy. The rocks, the icy crevasses
      - each one of her deliberate designs.
    - Over many generations, the Monks developed unique techniques for traversing
      the Mountain terrain that themselves resemble a form of meditation.
    - These techniques are now known as <color=#D0C4FF>Lotus Forms</color>.
    - There are many <color=#D0C4FF>Lotus Forms</color>, varying in function and
      difficulty.
    - I am no master, but it would be my pleasure to share with you a basic one.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    resetDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - The Tinsica is the form most people learn first. It's quite a versatile motion.
    - It engages the upper body, which is often neglected when running.
    - Practice consistently, and you may be able to learn more advanced <color=#D0C4FF>Lotus
      Forms</color>, though you will need to learn them from somewhere else.
    - I have taught you all I am able.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    resetDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - ...Mynkecha? Oh, right.
    - Mynkecha is a holy pilgrimage to the Summit. In ascending the Mountain, one's
      physical and spiritual resolve are tested.
    - Lotus Monks would peform their Mynkecha when they turned fourteen years of
      age. Can you believe that?
    - If only I had a fraction of their skill!
    advanceDialogueIndex: 1
    resetDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  - texts:
    - I think I need to meditate here a bit longer. It was a pleasure speaking with
      you.
    - Good luck on your climb.
    advanceDialogueIndex: 0
    resetDialogueIndex: 0
    canvasDelayOffset: 0
  DialogueName: Rheal
  LookAtOverride: {fileID: 0}
  CameraY: 0.5
  canvasDelay: 0
  cameraFollowOffsetLerp: 0
